            <!-- ─────────── §28.1 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="s28-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">28.1 Kubernetes Release Cycle</h3>
                <p>Understanding the release cycle helps you plan when and how to upgrade your cluster. Kubernetes follows a predictable release pattern.</p>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Kubernetes Version Numbering</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                    KUBERNETES VERSION FORMAT                                  │
  │                                                                              │
  │                         v1.31.2                                              │
  │                          │  │  │                                             │
  │                          │  │  └── PATCH version (bug fixes, security)       │
  │                          │  └──── MINOR version (new features)               │
  │                          └────── MAJOR version (always 1)                    │
  │                                                                              │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐         │
  │  │  RELEASE TIMELINE — Kubernetes Support Window                   │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  Time ──────────────────────────────────────────────▶           │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  v1.29  ████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░              │         │
  │  │         ◀── supported ─▶ ◀── end of life ──────▶               │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  v1.30  ░░░░████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░              │         │
  │  │              ◀── supported ─▶                                   │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  v1.31  ░░░░░░░░████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░              │         │
  │  │                  ◀── supported ─▶  ◀── current                  │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  v1.32  ░░░░░░░░░░░░████████████████                           │         │
  │  │                      ◀── latest ───▶                            │         │
  │  │                                                                 │         │
  │  │  📌 Only the latest 3 minor versions receive patches           │         │
  │  │  📌 Each minor version supported for ~14 months                │         │
  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘         │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Aspect</th>
                                <th>Minor Release</th>
                                <th>Patch Release</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Frequency</td><td>Every ~4 months</td><td>Monthly (or as needed)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>What changes</td><td>New features, API changes</td><td>Bug fixes, security patches</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Example</td><td>1.30 → 1.31</td><td>1.31.0 → 1.31.1</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Can you skip?</td><td>❌ No — upgrade one at a time</td><td>✅ Yes — jump from .0 to .3</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Downtime risk</td><td>Higher — requires drain/restart</td><td>Lower — kubelet restart only</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Planning needed</td><td>Read release notes, test first</td><td>Apply when available</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Component Version Skew Policy</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │              COMPONENT VERSION SKEW RULES                                    │
  │                                                                              │
  │   The API server is the "anchor" — everything else is relative to it        │
  │                                                                              │
  │   ┌─────────────────┐                                                       │
  │   │  kube-apiserver  │  ◀── THIS sets the version baseline                  │
  │   │    v1.31         │                                                       │
  │   └────────┬────────┘                                                       │
  │            │                                                                 │
  │   ┌────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┐                  │
  │   │        │  ALLOWED VERSION RANGES                      │                  │
  │   │        │                                              │                  │
  │   │  kubelet:         v1.30 or v1.31  (N-1 to N)         │                  │
  │   │  kube-proxy:      v1.30 or v1.31  (N-1 to N)         │                  │
  │   │  controller-mgr:  v1.31 only      (must match)       │                  │
  │   │  scheduler:       v1.31 only      (must match)       │                  │
  │   │  kubectl:         v1.30 to v1.32  (N-1 to N+1)      │                  │
  │   │                                                       │                  │
  │   │  ⚠️ kubelet CANNOT be newer than API server!          │                  │
  │   │  ⚠️ This is why you upgrade control plane FIRST!      │                  │
  │   └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                  │
  │                                                                              │
  │   EXAMPLE: API server at v1.31                                               │
  │   ┌──────────┬───────────────┬──────────────┐                               │
  │   │Component │  OK Versions  │  NOT OK      │                               │
  │   ├──────────┼───────────────┼──────────────┤                               │
  │   │kubelet   │ 1.30, 1.31    │ 1.29, 1.32   │                               │
  │   │kubectl   │ 1.30,1.31,1.32│ 1.29         │                               │
  │   │scheduler │ 1.31          │ 1.30, 1.32   │                               │
  │   └──────────┴───────────────┴──────────────┘                               │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Why Control Plane First?</h5>
                    <p>kubelet can be <strong>one minor version behind</strong> the API server, but <strong>never ahead</strong>. If you upgrade workers first, the kubelet would be v1.31 while the API server is still v1.30 — this violates the skew policy and causes unpredictable behavior. Always: <strong>control plane → workers</strong>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §28.2 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="s28-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">28.2 Upgrade Strategy</h3>
                <p>A cluster upgrade follows a strict sequence. Think of it as a conveyor belt — each step must complete before the next begins.</p>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Complete Cluster Upgrade Workflow — 10 Steps</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │         CLUSTER UPGRADE — COMPLETE WORKFLOW                                  │
  │                                                                              │
  │  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════              │
  │  PHASE 1: CONTROL PLANE UPGRADE                                              │
  │  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════              │
  │                                                                              │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 1: Upgrade kubeadm             │                                    │
  │  │ apt-mark unhold kubeadm             │                                    │
  │  │ apt-get install kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1  │                                    │
  │  │ apt-mark hold kubeadm               │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 2: Check upgrade plan          │                                    │
  │  │ kubeadm upgrade plan                │                                    │
  │  │ (shows available target versions)   │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 3: Apply upgrade               │  ◀── This upgrades API server,    │
  │  │ kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0       │      controller-mgr, scheduler,   │
  │  │                                     │      kube-proxy, CoreDNS, etcd     │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 4: Drain control plane node    │                                    │
  │  │ kubectl drain controlplane          │                                    │
  │  │   --ignore-daemonsets               │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 5: Upgrade kubelet + kubectl   │                                    │
  │  │ apt-get install kubelet=1.31.0-1.1  │                                    │
  │  │                kubectl=1.31.0-1.1   │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 6: Restart kubelet             │                                    │
  │  │ systemctl daemon-reload             │                                    │
  │  │ systemctl restart kubelet           │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 7: Uncordon control plane      │                                    │
  │  │ kubectl uncordon controlplane       │                                    │
  │  └─────────────────────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                                                                              │
  │  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════              │
  │  PHASE 2: WORKER NODE UPGRADE (repeat for EACH worker)                       │
  │  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════              │
  │                                                                              │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 8: Drain worker                │  ◀── Run from control plane       │
  │  │ kubectl drain worker01              │                                    │
  │  │   --ignore-daemonsets               │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 9: SSH to worker + upgrade     │  ◀── Run ON the worker node       │
  │  │ apt-get install kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1  │                                    │
  │  │ kubeadm upgrade node                │  ◀── NOT "upgrade apply"!         │
  │  │ apt-get install kubelet=1.31.0-1.1  │                                    │
  │  │ systemctl daemon-reload             │                                    │
  │  │ systemctl restart kubelet           │                                    │
  │  └──────────────┬──────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                 ▼                                                            │
  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                                    │
  │  │ STEP 10: Uncordon worker            │  ◀── Run from control plane       │
  │  │ kubectl uncordon worker01           │                                    │
  │  │ kubectl get nodes (verify Ready)    │                                    │
  │  └─────────────────────────────────────┘                                    │
  │                                                                              │
  │  💡 Repeat Steps 8-10 for worker02, worker03, etc.                          │
  │  💡 Upgrade one worker at a time to maintain app availability!              │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="card-grid cols-3">
                    <div class="info-card highlight">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🔧</div>
                        <h5>apt-mark hold</h5>
                        <p>Prevents apt from auto-upgrading kubeadm, kubelet, or kubectl during <code>apt-get upgrade</code>. Always hold after installing.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card highlight">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📋</div>
                        <h5>kubeadm upgrade plan</h5>
                        <p>Shows available upgrade targets, pre-flight checks, and component versions. Run this BEFORE applying to verify everything is ready.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card highlight">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🔄</div>
                        <h5>daemon-reload</h5>
                        <p>Tells systemd to re-read unit files. Required after upgrading kubelet binary — without it, systemd runs the OLD version.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="scenario-box positive">
                        <h5>✅ Upgrade Best Practices</h5>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Always backup etcd BEFORE upgrading</strong> (Chapter 29)</li>
                            <li>Read release notes for breaking changes</li>
                            <li>Test upgrade in a staging cluster first</li>
                            <li>Upgrade one minor version at a time</li>
                            <li>Upgrade workers one at a time for availability</li>
                            <li>Verify <code>kubectl get nodes</code> shows correct version after each node</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scenario-box">
                        <h5>❌ Upgrade Anti-Patterns</h5>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Skipping minor versions (1.30 → 1.32)</li>
                            <li>Upgrading all workers simultaneously</li>
                            <li>Forgetting to drain before upgrading</li>
                            <li>Not running <code>kubeadm upgrade plan</code> first</li>
                            <li>Skipping <code>systemctl daemon-reload</code></li>
                            <li>Not holding packages after install</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📌 easypj Upgrade Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Your <strong>easypj</strong> job board runs 3 replicas across 2 worker nodes. When you drain <code>worker01</code>, Kubernetes evicts the easypj pods and the Deployment controller reschedules them on <code>worker02</code>. With a PodDisruptionBudget (Chapter 30) of <code>minAvailable: 2</code>, the drain ensures at least 2 replicas stay running throughout the upgrade.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Pre-Upgrade Checklist -->
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">✅ Pre-Upgrade Checklist — Before You Touch Anything</div>
                    <pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  PRE-UPGRADE CHECKLIST (CKA &amp; Production)                │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                          │
│  □ 1. CHECK current versions                                             │
│       kubectl get nodes                                                  │
│       kubeadm version                                                    │
│       kubelet --version                                                  │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 2. BACKUP etcd (see Chapter 29)                                       │
│       ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot save /opt/pre-upgrade-backup.db \   │
│         --endpoints=... --cacert=... --cert=... --key=...                │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 3. READ the release notes                                             │
│       Check for removed APIs, deprecated features, breaking changes      │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 4. VERIFY cluster health                                              │
│       kubectl get cs            (component status — deprecated but useful)│
│       kubectl get nodes         (all nodes Ready?)                       │
│       kubectl get pods -A       (any pods in CrashLoop or Pending?)      │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 5. CHECK available versions                                           │
│       apt-cache madison kubeadm (see available versions in repo)         │
│       kubeadm upgrade plan      (see upgrade targets)                    │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 6. CONFIRM you're upgrading ONE minor version                         │
│       Current: v1.30.x → Target: v1.31.x ✅                             │
│       Current: v1.30.x → Target: v1.32.x ❌ (skip not allowed!)        │
│                                                                          │
│  □ 7. VERIFY sufficient capacity                                         │
│       Can remaining nodes handle ALL pods while one is being upgraded?   │
│       kubectl top nodes (check CPU/memory headroom)                      │
│                                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </pre>
                </div>

                <!-- Component Upgrade Order -->
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <h4>📋 Upgrade Order — What Gets Upgraded When</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Step</th>
                                <th>Component</th>
                                <th>Where</th>
                                <th>Command</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>1</strong></td>
                                <td>kubeadm</td>
                                <td>Control plane</td>
                                <td><code>apt-get install kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>2</strong></td>
                                <td>Control plane components</td>
                                <td>Control plane</td>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>3</strong></td>
                                <td>kubelet + kubectl</td>
                                <td>Control plane</td>
                                <td><code>apt-get install kubelet=... kubectl=...</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>4</strong></td>
                                <td>kubeadm</td>
                                <td>Each worker (one at a time)</td>
                                <td><code>apt-get install kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>5</strong></td>
                                <td>Node config</td>
                                <td>Each worker</td>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade node</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>6</strong></td>
                                <td>kubelet + kubectl</td>
                                <td>Each worker</td>
                                <td><code>apt-get install kubelet=... kubectl=...</code></td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

            </section>

            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- Section 28.3 — Hands-On: Upgrading the Control Plane       -->
            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- ─────────── §28.3 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="s28-3">                    <h3 class="section-h">28.3 Hands-On: Upgrading the Control Plane</h3>
                    <span class="badge badge-exam">🎯 CKA EXAM TOPIC</span>

                <p>This is the <strong>exact workflow</strong> you'll perform on the CKA exam. Every command below maps directly to what the exam environment expects. Practice this sequence until it becomes muscle memory.</p>

                <!-- Control Plane Upgrade Flow Diagram -->
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">🔧 Control Plane Upgrade — Complete Command Flow</div>
                    <pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  CONTROL PLANE NODE UPGRADE PROCEDURE                    │
│                  (SSH into control-plane node first)                      │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                          │
│  PHASE 1 ─ UPGRADE kubeadm                                              │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Step 1: Unhold kubeadm package                                    │   │
│  │ $ apt-mark unhold kubeadm                                         │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 2: Install target kubeadm version                            │   │
│  │ $ apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1         │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 3: Hold kubeadm to prevent auto-updates                      │   │
│  │ $ apt-mark hold kubeadm                                           │   │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                               │                                          │
│                               ▼                                          │
│  PHASE 2 ─ PLAN & APPLY                                                 │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Step 4: Verify upgrade plan (shows available versions)            │   │
│  │ $ kubeadm upgrade plan                                            │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 5: Apply the upgrade to control plane                        │   │
│  │ $ kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0                                   │   │
│  │         ▲                                                          │   │
│  │         └─ ONLY on first control-plane node!                      │   │
│  │            Additional control planes use: kubeadm upgrade node    │   │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                               │                                          │
│                               ▼                                          │
│  PHASE 3 ─ DRAIN & UPGRADE kubelet                                      │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Step 6: Drain the control plane node                              │   │
│  │ $ kubectl drain controlplane --ignore-daemonsets                   │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 7: Upgrade kubelet & kubectl                                 │   │
│  │ $ apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl                                 │   │
│  │ $ apt-get update && apt-get install -y \                          │   │
│  │       kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1                      │   │
│  │ $ apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl                                   │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 8: Restart kubelet                                           │   │
│  │ $ systemctl daemon-reload                                         │   │
│  │ $ systemctl restart kubelet                                       │   │
│  │         ▲                                                          │   │
│  │         └─ ⚠️ BOTH commands required! daemon-reload first!       │   │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                               │                                          │
│                               ▼                                          │
│  PHASE 4 ─ VERIFY & UNCORDON                                            │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Step 9: Mark node schedulable again                               │   │
│  │ $ kubectl uncordon controlplane                                   │   │
│  │                                                                    │   │
│  │ Step 10: Verify upgrade                                           │   │
│  │ $ kubectl get nodes                                               │   │
│  │ NAME           STATUS   ROLES           VERSION                   │   │
│  │ controlplane   Ready    control-plane   v1.31.0  ← ✅ Updated   │   │
│  │ worker01       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          v1.30.0  ← Still old    │   │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </pre>
                </div>

                <!-- Step-by-step code blocks -->
                <h4>Step 1–3: Upgrade kubeadm Package</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">control-plane-node (SSH)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 1: Unhold kubeadm so we can upgrade it</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Step 2: Update repositories and install target version</span>
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1

<span class="comment"># Step 3: Hold kubeadm again to prevent accidental updates</span>
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Verify kubeadm version</span>
kubeadm version</code></pre>
                </div>

                <h4>Step 4–5: Plan and Apply the Upgrade</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">control-plane-node (SSH)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 4: Check what upgrade is available</span>
kubeadm upgrade plan
<span class="comment"># Shows: Components that will be upgraded</span>
<span class="comment">#        Available versions</span>
<span class="comment">#        Any manual actions needed</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 5: Apply the upgrade (FIRST control-plane only!)</span>
kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0
<span class="comment"># ⚠️ For additional control-plane nodes, use:</span>
<span class="comment">#    kubeadm upgrade node</span></code></pre>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ apply vs node — Critical Distinction</h5>
                    <p><code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code> — Used on the <strong>first</strong> control-plane node. Downloads new component images and upgrades the cluster configuration.</p>
                    <p><code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> — Used on <strong>additional</strong> control-plane nodes AND <strong>all worker nodes</strong>. Only updates local kubelet config.</p>
                </div>

                <h4>Step 6–8: Drain, Upgrade kubelet, Restart</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">control-plane-node (SSH)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 6: Drain the node (evict workloads, mark unschedulable)</span>
kubectl drain controlplane --ignore-daemonsets

<span class="comment"># Step 7: Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

<span class="comment"># Step 8: Reload systemd config and restart kubelet</span>
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl restart kubelet</code></pre>
                </div>

                <div class="cka-gotcha">
                    <h5>⚠️ Exam Trap: Forgetting daemon-reload</h5>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>❌ Wrong</th><th>✅ Correct</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>systemctl restart kubelet</code> (only)</td>
                                <td><code>systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kubelet</code></td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p>After upgrading the kubelet binary, systemd still has the old unit file cached. Without <code>daemon-reload</code>, the restart may use the old configuration or fail silently.</p>
                </div>

                <h4>Step 9–10: Uncordon and Verify</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">control-plane-node (SSH)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 9: Make node schedulable again</span>
kubectl uncordon controlplane

<span class="comment"># Step 10: Verify upgrade succeeded</span>
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># Expected output:</span>
<span class="comment"># NAME           STATUS   ROLES           AGE   VERSION</span>
<span class="comment"># controlplane   Ready    control-plane   45d   v1.31.0</span>
<span class="comment"># worker01       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          45d   v1.30.0</span></code></pre>
                </div>

                <!-- Complete single-copy command -->
                <div class="info-box tip">
                    <h5>💡 Complete Control Plane Upgrade — Copy-Paste Block</h5>
                    <p>Run these commands in order on the control plane node. Replace version numbers with your target:</p>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">full-control-plane-upgrade.sh</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash">#!/bin/bash
<span class="comment"># === COMPLETE CONTROL PLANE UPGRADE (v1.30 → v1.31) ===</span>
TARGET=1.31.0-1.1
TARGET_SHORT=v1.31.0

<span class="comment"># 1. Upgrade kubeadm</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=${TARGET}
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># 2. Plan and apply</span>
kubeadm upgrade plan
kubeadm upgrade apply ${TARGET_SHORT}

<span class="comment"># 3. Drain, upgrade kubelet, restart</span>
kubectl drain controlplane --ignore-daemonsets
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=${TARGET} kubectl=${TARGET}
apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># 4. Uncordon and verify</span>
kubectl uncordon controlplane
kubectl get nodes</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- Section 28.4 — Hands-On: Upgrading Worker Nodes            -->
            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- ─────────── §28.4 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="s28-4">                    <h3 class="section-h">28.4 Hands-On: Upgrading Worker Nodes</h3>
                    <span class="badge badge-exam">🎯 CKA EXAM TOPIC</span>

                <p>After the control plane is upgraded, each worker node must be upgraded <strong>one at a time</strong> to maintain application availability. The process involves commands on <strong>two different nodes</strong> — pay close attention to <em>where</em> each command runs.</p>

                <!-- Worker Upgrade Flow Diagram -->
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">🔧 Worker Node Upgrade — Two-Node Command Flow</div>
                    <pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              WORKER NODE UPGRADE — WHERE EACH COMMAND RUNS               │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                          │
│  🖥️ FROM CONTROL PLANE                  🖥️ SSH INTO WORKER NODE        │
│  ┌─────────────────────────┐            ┌─────────────────────────┐     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  │ Step 1: Drain worker    │            │                         │     │
│  │ $ kubectl drain \       │            │                         │     │
│  │   worker01 \            │            │                         │     │
│  │   --ignore-daemonsets \ │            │                         │     │
│  │   --delete-emptydir-data│            │                         │     │
│  │                         │───────────▶│ Step 2: SSH to worker   │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ ssh worker01          │     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  │                         │            │ Step 3: Upgrade kubeadm │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-mark unhold \     │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubeadm               │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-get update && \   │     │
│  │                         │            │   apt-get install -y \  │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1    │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-mark hold kubeadm │     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  │                         │            │ Step 4: Upgrade node    │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ kubeadm upgrade node  │     │
│  │                         │            │   ▲                     │     │
│  │                         │            │   └─ NOT "apply"!       │     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  │                         │            │ Step 5: Upgrade kubelet │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-mark unhold \     │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubelet kubectl       │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-get install -y \  │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 \  │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubectl=1.31.0-1.1    │     │
│  │                         │            │ $ apt-mark hold \       │     │
│  │                         │            │   kubelet kubectl       │     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  │                         │            │ Step 6: Restart kubelet │     │
│  │                         │◀───────────│ $ systemctl daemon- \   │     │
│  │                         │            │   reload                │     │
│  │ Step 7: Uncordon        │            │ $ systemctl restart \   │     │
│  │ $ kubectl uncordon \    │            │   kubelet               │     │
│  │   worker01              │            │ $ exit                  │     │
│  │                         │            │                         │     │
│  └─────────────────────────┘            └─────────────────────────┘     │
│                                                                          │
│  Step 8: Verify     $ kubectl get nodes                                  │
│  NAME           STATUS   ROLES           VERSION                         │
│  controlplane   Ready    control-plane   v1.31.0  ✅                    │
│  worker01       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          v1.31.0  ✅                    │
│  worker02       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          v1.30.0  ← next               │
│                                                                          │
│  🔁 REPEAT Steps 1–8 for worker02, worker03, etc.                       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </pre>
                </div>

                <!-- Comparison Table: Control Plane vs Worker -->
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <h4>📊 Control Plane vs Worker Node Upgrade — Key Differences</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Aspect</th>
                                <th>Control Plane (First)</th>
                                <th>Worker Node</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>kubeadm command</strong></td>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code></td>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade node</code></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Drain from</strong></td>
                                <td>Same node (self-drain)</td>
                                <td>Control plane (remote drain)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>What it upgrades</strong></td>
                                <td>API server, controller-manager, scheduler, etcd</td>
                                <td>kubelet config only</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Order</strong></td>
                                <td>Must be upgraded FIRST</td>
                                <td>After ALL control planes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Parallelism</strong></td>
                                <td>One at a time (HA: first with apply, rest with node)</td>
                                <td>One at a time for availability</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>kubelet/kubectl</strong></td>
                                <td>Must upgrade + restart</td>
                                <td>Must upgrade + restart</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <!-- Step-by-step code for worker -->
                <h4>From Control Plane — Drain the Worker</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">controlplane (kubectl)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Drain the worker node from control plane</span>
kubectl drain worker01 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data

<span class="comment"># Verify pods have been evicted</span>
kubectl get pods -o wide | grep worker01
<span class="comment"># Should show no pods (except DaemonSets)</span></code></pre>
                </div>

                <h4>On Worker Node — Upgrade Components</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">worker01 (SSH)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># SSH into the worker node</span>
ssh worker01

<span class="comment"># Upgrade kubeadm</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Apply node upgrade (NOT "apply" — that's for first control-plane only!)</span>
kubeadm upgrade node

<span class="comment"># Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

<span class="comment"># Restart kubelet (BOTH commands required!)</span>
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># Exit back to control plane</span>
exit</code></pre>
                </div>

                <h4>Back on Control Plane — Uncordon and Verify</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">controlplane (kubectl)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Make worker schedulable again</span>
kubectl uncordon worker01

<span class="comment"># Verify ALL nodes are Ready and on correct version</span>
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># NAME           STATUS   ROLES           AGE   VERSION</span>
<span class="comment"># controlplane   Ready    control-plane   45d   v1.31.0</span>
<span class="comment"># worker01       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          45d   v1.31.0  ← ✅</span>
<span class="comment"># worker02       Ready    &lt;none&gt;          45d   v1.30.0</span>

<span class="comment"># Repeat for worker02:</span>
<span class="comment"># kubectl drain worker02 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data</span>
<span class="comment"># ssh worker02 → same upgrade steps → exit</span>
<span class="comment"># kubectl uncordon worker02</span></code></pre>
                </div>

                <!-- easypj scenario -->
                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📌 easypj Worker Upgrade — What Happens to Your Pods</h5>
                    <p>When you drain <code>worker01</code> where 2 of 3 easypj replicas run:</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>The 2 easypj pods on worker01 receive <code>SIGTERM</code> and begin graceful shutdown</li>
                        <li>The Deployment controller detects 2 missing replicas and creates replacements</li>
                        <li>The scheduler places both new pods on <code>worker02</code> (the only available node)</li>
                        <li>Your PDB (<code>minAvailable: 2</code>) ensures at least 2 replicas stay running throughout</li>
                        <li>After you uncordon worker01, the scheduler can use it again for future pod scheduling</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>

                <div class="cka-gotcha">
                    <h5>⚠️ Exam Trap: apply vs node on Workers</h5>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>❌ Wrong</th><th>✅ Correct</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code> (on worker)</td>
                                <td><code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> (on worker)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p>Using <code>apply</code> on a worker node will fail or cause unexpected behavior. Only the <strong>first</strong> control-plane node uses <code>apply</code>. All other nodes (additional control-planes AND workers) use <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- Chapter 28 — Practice Drills                               -->
            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <div class="cka-practice-drill" id="s28-drill-1">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.1 — Upgrade the Control Plane</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 8 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Your cluster is running Kubernetes v1.30.0. You need to upgrade the <strong>control plane node</strong> named <code>controlplane</code> to v1.31.0. Complete the full upgrade process.</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Upgrade kubeadm to 1.31.0-1.1 on the control plane</li>
                        <li>Run the upgrade plan and apply the upgrade</li>
                        <li>Drain the control plane node</li>
                        <li>Upgrade kubelet and kubectl to 1.31.0-1.1</li>
                        <li>Restart kubelet and uncordon the node</li>
                        <li>Verify the control plane shows v1.31.0</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Remember the order — kubeadm first, then plan/apply, then drain, then kubelet/kubectl. Don't forget <code>apt-mark hold</code> after each install and <code>daemon-reload</code> before restart.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># On controlplane node:</span>

<span class="comment"># 1. Upgrade kubeadm</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># 2. Plan and apply</span>
kubeadm upgrade plan
kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0

<span class="comment"># 3. Drain</span>
kubectl drain controlplane --ignore-daemonsets

<span class="comment"># 4. Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

<span class="comment"># 5. Restart kubelet</span>
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># 6. Uncordon and verify</span>
kubectl uncordon controlplane
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># controlplane should show v1.31.0</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-practice-drill" id="s28-drill-2">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.2 — Upgrade a Worker Node</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 6 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>The control plane is already on v1.31.0. Now upgrade worker node <code>worker01</code> to v1.31.0. Remember: commands run on <strong>two different nodes</strong>.</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Drain worker01 from the control plane</li>
                        <li>SSH into worker01 and upgrade kubeadm</li>
                        <li>Run kubeadm upgrade node (not apply!)</li>
                        <li>Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</li>
                        <li>Restart kubelet and exit back to control plane</li>
                        <li>Uncordon worker01 and verify all nodes</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> On workers, use <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> — NOT <code>kubeadm upgrade apply</code>. The drain and uncordon commands run from the control plane, not the worker.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># FROM CONTROL PLANE:</span>
kubectl drain worker01 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data

<span class="comment"># SSH INTO WORKER01:</span>
ssh worker01

<span class="comment"># Upgrade kubeadm</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Upgrade node config (NOT apply!)</span>
kubeadm upgrade node

<span class="comment"># Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

<span class="comment"># Restart kubelet</span>
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl restart kubelet
exit

<span class="comment"># BACK ON CONTROL PLANE:</span>
kubectl uncordon worker01
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># worker01 should show v1.31.0</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-practice-drill" id="s28-drill-3">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.3 — Find the Correct Package Version</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 2 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>You need to upgrade your cluster but aren't sure what package versions are available. Find all available kubeadm versions for 1.31 in the apt repository.</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>List available kubeadm versions using apt-cache</li>
                        <li>Identify the correct version string to use with <code>apt-get install</code></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Use <code>apt-cache madison</code> to list available package versions from repositories.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># List all available versions of kubeadm</span>
apt-cache madison kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Example output:</span>
<span class="comment">#    kubeadm |  1.31.0-1.1 | https://pkgs.k8s.io/...</span>
<span class="comment">#    kubeadm |  1.30.4-1.1 | https://pkgs.k8s.io/...</span>
<span class="comment">#    kubeadm |  1.30.0-1.1 | https://pkgs.k8s.io/...</span>

<span class="comment"># The version string to use is the second column: 1.31.0-1.1</span>
<span class="comment"># Usage: apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Chapter 28 Verification Checklist -->
            <div class="cka-verify">
                <h4>✅ Chapter 28 — Verification Checklist</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><code>kubectl get nodes</code> — All nodes show expected version</li>
                    <li><code>kubeadm version</code> — kubeadm matches target version</li>
                    <li><code>kubelet --version</code> — kubelet matches target version</li>
                    <li><code>kubectl version --short</code> — kubectl matches target version</li>
                    <li><code>kubectl get pods -n kube-system</code> — All control plane pods running</li>
                    <li><code>kubectl get nodes -o wide</code> — All nodes Ready, no SchedulingDisabled</li>
                    <li><code>apt-mark showhold</code> — kubeadm, kubelet, kubectl are held</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

                <!-- CKA Augmentation: Chapter 28 -->
                <div class="cka-gotcha">
                    <h5>⚠️ CKA Gotcha: Cluster Upgrade Traps</h5>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Upgrade order is rigid</strong> — Always: kubeadm → control plane → kubelet+kubectl → worker nodes. Never upgrade workers before the control plane. Never skip minor versions (1.30→1.32 is NOT allowed, must go 1.30→1.31→1.32)</li>
                        <li><strong>Drain before upgrading workers</strong> — <code>kubectl drain &lt;node&gt; --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data</code>. Forgetting <code>--ignore-daemonsets</code> causes the drain to fail. Forgetting to drain means workloads crash during kubelet restart</li>
                        <li><strong><code>apt-mark hold</code> after install</strong> — Always hold kubeadm, kubelet, kubectl after upgrading: <code>apt-mark hold kubeadm kubelet kubectl</code>. This prevents accidental upgrades via <code>apt upgrade</code></li>
                        <li><strong>Control plane static pods restart automatically</strong> — After <code>kubeadm upgrade apply</code>, the API server, controller-manager, and scheduler restart. There's a brief disruption — the exam expects you to know this</li>
                        <li><strong>Version skew policy</strong> — kubelet can be up to 3 minor versions behind the API server. kubectl can be ±1 minor version. kube-proxy must match kubelet. The exam tests awareness of these constraints</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>


                <div class="cka-imperative-ref">
                    <strong>⚡ Upgrade commands:</strong>
                    <code>kubeadm upgrade plan</code> — shows available upgrade targets<br>
                    <code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code> — upgrade control plane (first node only)<br>
                    <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> — upgrade additional control planes and workers<br>
                    <code>kubectl get nodes</code> — verify versions after upgrade<br>
                    <code>apt-cache madison kubeadm</code> — find available package versions
                </div>

                <!-- ═══ UTH Chapter 28 — How kubeadm upgrade Actually Works ═══ -->

                <!-- Chapter 28 Exam Questions -->

            <!-- ─────────── UNDER THE HOOD ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth"><summary>Under the Hood — How kubeadm upgrade Actually Works: Component-by-Component Version Bump, Static Pod Manifest Updates, and Node Drain Sequencing</summary>
            <div class="uth-body">
            <h5>🗺️ Cluster Upgrade — The Complete Sequence</h5>
            <p><code>kubeadm upgrade</code> doesn't upgrade running containers in-place. It updates static pod manifests AND upgrades kubelet/kubectl binaries. Understanding the exact sequence prevents catastrophic upgrade failures.</p>
            <div class="uth-diagram"><pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CLUSTER UPGRADE — Full Sequence (1.30.0 → 1.31.0)                           │
│                                                                              │
│  PHASE 1: UPGRADE CONTROL PLANE NODE (cp-node-1)                             │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ 1. DRAIN the node (move workloads to other nodes):                   │   │
│  │    $ kubectl drain cp-node-1 --ignore-daemonsets                      │   │
│  │    → All pods evicted to other nodes                                  │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │ 2. UPGRADE kubeadm binary:                                            │   │
│  │    $ sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm                                     │   │
│  │    $ sudo apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-*     │   │
│  │    $ sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm                                       │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │ 3. UPGRADE control plane (kubeadm updates static pod manifests):     │   │
│  │    $ sudo kubeadm upgrade plan   <span class="comment">← SEE what will change              </span>│   │
│  │    $ sudo kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0                               │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │    kubeadm upgrade apply DOES:                                        │   │
│  │    ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │   │
│  │    │ • Update /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml     │    │   │
│  │    │   → image: registry.k8s.io/kube-apiserver:v1.30.0          │    │   │
│  │    │                        ↓                                   │    │   │
│  │    │   → image: registry.k8s.io/kube-apiserver:v1.31.0          │    │   │
│  │    │                                                              │    │   │
│  │    │ • Same for: kube-controller-manager.yaml, kube-scheduler.yaml│    │   │
│  │    │ • Update kubeadm-config + kubelet-config ConfigMaps         │    │   │
│  │    │ • Renew certificates if close to expiry                     │    │   │
│  │    │ • Add new API resources for v1.31 (if any)                  │    │   │
│  │    │                                                              │    │   │
│  │    │ ⚡ KUBELET DETECTS manifest changes → restarts static pods  │    │   │
│  │    │ ⚡ New API Server starts with v1.31.0 image                 │    │   │
│  │    └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │ 4. UPGRADE kubelet + kubectl on this node:                           │   │
│  │    $ sudo apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-* kubectl=1.31.0-*     │   │
│  │    $ sudo systemctl daemon-reload                                     │   │
│  │    $ sudo systemctl restart kubelet                                   │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │ 5. UNCORDON the node:                                                 │   │
│  │    $ kubectl uncordon cp-node-1                                        │   │
│  │    → Node is schedulable again                                         │   │
│  │                                                                       │   │
│  │ 6. VERIFY:                                                             │   │
│  │    $ kubectl get nodes                                                │   │
│  │    cp-node-1   Ready   control-plane   v1.31.0 ✅                    │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                              │
│  PHASE 2: UPGRADE WORKER NODES (for EACH worker)                             │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ 1. DRAIN worker: kubectl drain worker-1 --ignore-daemonsets           │   │
│  │ 2. Upgrade kubeadm: apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-*              │   │
│  │ 3. Upgrade node: sudo kubeadm upgrade node                            │   │
│  │    → Updates kubelet-config, NOT static pod manifests (worker)       │   │
│  │ 4. Upgrade kubelet: apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-*              │   │
│  │ 5. Restart kubelet: sudo systemctl restart kubelet                    │   │
│  │ 6. Uncordon: kubectl uncordon worker-1                                │   │
│  │ 7. Repeat for each worker                                             │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                              │
│  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════     │
│  VERSION SKEW POLICY (CKA Critical):                                         │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ • kube-apiserver must be at version X or X+1 (can be 1 ahead)        │   │
│  │ • kubelet/kube-proxy must be at version X or X-1 (1 behind allowed)  │   │
│  │ • kubectl: X or X+1 or X-1 (1 version skew in either direction)      │   │
│  │                                                                        │   │
│  │ Upgrade ORDER (MUST follow):                                          │   │
│  │   1. Control Plane FIRST                                              │   │
│  │   2. Workers AFTER (one at a time, drain before each)                │   │
│  │                                                                        │   │
│  │ NEVER skip minor versions: 1.30 → 1.31 → 1.32 (NOT 1.30 → 1.32)     │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre></div>
            <div class="uth-callout">
            <strong>🔑 CKA Insight:</strong> Cluster upgrade is a GUARANTEED CKA exam question. Memorize the sequence: drain→upgrade kubeadm→upgrade apply (cp) or upgrade node (worker)→upgrade kubelet→restart→uncordon. Common traps: forgetting to hold packages after upgrade, draining without --ignore-daemonsets (blocks on DaemonSet pods), and skipping version skew policy (always upgrade one minor at a time).
            </div>
            </div>
            </details>

            <!-- ─────────── KEY TAKEAWAYS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="chapter-placeholder">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <p>Bulleted key takeaways go here.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── GOTCHAS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li>❌ <span class="gotcha-wrong">Skip from 1.30 to 1.32 directly</span></li>
                    <li>✅ <span class="gotcha-correct">Upgrade one minor version at a time: 1.30 → 1.31 → 1.32</span></li>
                    <li>❌ <span class="gotcha-wrong">Upgrade workers before control plane</span></li>
                    <li>✅ <span class="gotcha-correct">Always upgrade control plane FIRST, then workers</span></li>
                    <li>❌ <span class="gotcha-wrong">Forget <code>systemctl daemon-reload</code> after upgrading kubelet</span></li>
                    <li>✅ <span class="gotcha-correct">Always run <code>systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kubelet</code></span></li>
                    <li>On workers use <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code>, NOT <code>kubeadm upgrade apply</code></li>
                    <li><code>--ignore-daemonsets</code> is REQUIRED on drain — DaemonSet pods can't be evicted</li>
                    <li>Check the package version format — some providers use <code>=1.31.0-1.1</code> not <code>=1.31.0-00</code></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── SPEED TIPS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-speed"></span>
            <div class="cka-speed-tip">
                <h5>⚡ Speed Tips</h5>
                <p><strong>CKA Speed Tip — Upgrade workflow memorization:</strong><br>
                <strong>Control plane:</strong><br>
                <code>apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1</code><br>
                <code>kubeadm upgrade plan</code> → <code>kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0</code><br>
                <code>apt-get install -y kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1</code><br>
                <code>systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kubelet</code><br>
                <strong>Worker:</strong><br>
                <code>kubectl drain &lt;node&gt; --ignore-daemonsets</code> (from control plane)<br>
                SSH to worker → upgrade kubeadm → <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> → upgrade kubelet → restart<br>
                <code>kubectl uncordon &lt;node&gt;</code> (from control plane)</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── COMMANDS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-commands"></span>
            <div class="chapter-placeholder">
                <h4>🔑 Commands to Know (Chapter 28)</h4>
                <p>The command reference for this chapter goes here.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── PRACTICE DRILL ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-drill"></span>
