            <div class="chapter-intro">
                <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 39 · Security Hardening &amp; Best Practices</h2>
                <p class="chapter-lead">A comprehensive security hardening guide covering RBAC best practices, Secrets management, API server security, supply chain security, runtime protection with seccomp/AppArmor, and multi-tenancy isolation — all demonstrated with the <strong>easypj</strong> Django project.</p>
                <div class="chapter-meta">
                    <span class="meta-tag">🔴 Advanced</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~3 hours</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">🔒 Security</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">📝 CKA EXAM</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="learning-objectives">
                <h4>🎯 What You'll Learn</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>✅ <strong>RBAC Hardening</strong> — principle of least privilege, avoiding dangerous permissions</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Secrets Best Practices</strong> — encryption at rest, external secret stores, avoiding anti-patterns</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>API Server Security</strong> — audit logging, anonymous auth, admission control</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Supply Chain Security</strong> — image scanning, signed images, allowlisting registries</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Runtime Security</strong> — seccomp profiles, AppArmor, read-only filesystems</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Network Hardening</strong> — default-deny policies, egress filtering, service mesh</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Multi-Tenancy</strong> — namespace isolation, resource quotas, network boundaries</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-chapter-relevance">
                <span class="relevance-label">CKA Exam Relevance</span>
