                <h5>Security on the CKA Exam</h5>
                <p>Security topics appear across multiple CKA domains. You may be asked to <strong>create RBAC rules</strong>, <strong>configure network policies</strong>, <strong>troubleshoot Secret issues</strong>, or <strong>apply Pod Security Standards</strong>. This chapter consolidates all security knowledge into a hardening checklist you can follow during the exam.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>High Priority</strong> — RBAC (ClusterRole/Role, bindings), NetworkPolicy, Secrets encryption</li>
                    <li><strong>Medium Priority</strong> — Pod Security Admission, SecurityContext, ServiceAccount tokens</li>
                    <li><strong>Awareness</strong> — seccomp, AppArmor, audit logging, image security</li>
