            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch40-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="chapter-placeholder">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <p>Bulleted key takeaways go here.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── GOTCHAS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch40-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li>❌ <strong>Labels apply at namespace level only</strong> — you cannot apply PSA to individual pods, only entire namespaces</li>
                    <li>❌ <strong>Existing pods aren't evicted</strong> — enforce mode only blocks NEW pods. Existing violating pods continue running</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Use warn + audit first</strong> — apply warning mode before enforce to discover violations without breaking workloads</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Check with dry-run</strong> — <code>kubectl label --dry-run=server --overwrite ns easypj pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted</code> shows what would be blocked</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── SPEED TIPS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch40-speed"></span>
            <div class="cka-speed-tip">
                <h5>⚡ Speed Tips</h5>
                <p><strong>CKA Quick Reference</strong> — When a ResourceQuota exists in a namespace, ALL pods in that namespace MUST specify resource requests and limits. If they don't and no LimitRange provides defaults, the pod will be rejected. This is why LimitRange and ResourceQuota are often used together: LimitRange provides defaults so pods without explicit limits still get created.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── COMMANDS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch40-commands"></span>
            <div class="chapter-placeholder">
                <h4>🔑 Commands to Know (Chapter 40)</h4>
                <p>The command reference for this chapter goes here.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ─────────── PRACTICE DRILL ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch40-drill"></span>
